{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>For seven days shall he fill your hands.</b> So too the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him in the section of ואתה תצוה: שבעת ימים תמלא את ידם. <b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> the days of the ordination were seven, corresponding to the seven that are known. For you already know what the archetype of the high priest is, of whom Moses, peace be upon him, prophesied, in the manner of what is written (Isaiah 63:12): מוליך לימין משה זרוע תפארתו. And therefore Moses was commanded to attend to Aaron and to anoint him, for thus it mentioned above: ויצק משמן המשחה על ראש אהרן וימשח אתו לקדשו. And therefore they were called ימי מלואים, in the language of שלמות (perfection), for their archetype is the perfection of all. And you already know that Moses served all seven days of the ordination, and the inauguration of Aaron's priesthood was through Moses. And understand this."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:03.266841330Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}